  "title": "Erdős Problem #796",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $k\\geq 2$ and let $g_k(n)$ be the largest possible size of $A\\subseteq \\{1,\\ldots,n\\}$ such that every $m$ has $<k$ solutions to $m=a_1a_2$ with $a_1<a_2\\in A$.\nIs it true that $ g_3(n)=\\frac{\\log\\log n}{\\log n}n+(c+o(1))\\frac{n}{\\log n} $ for some constant $c$?",
